## Component Style Guide

Use this reference when writing or updating **CURSOR INFO** blocks on section and block components (especially the **VISUAL STYLE** field). Values should match the the component itself and disregard the site-design.mdc

### How to write VISUAL STYLE

- Use **short, comma-separated adjectives** (2–5 terms).
- **One line** in the CURSOR INFO block; no long paragraphs.
- Pick terms that describe how the section *looks*, not what it contains (layout and content belong in other fields).
- Put motion and behavior details (parallax, scroll animation) in **NOTES / MODIFIERS** unless they define the visual identity.

**Example:**

```ts
* VISUAL STYLE: Modern, minimal, luxury, and clean
```

### Primary styles (default vocabulary)

Best fit for this template. Prefer these unless a section intentionally breaks from the site aesthetic.

| Style | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| **Modern** | Default for most sections |
| **Minimal** | Generous whitespace, simple structure |
| **Clean** | Uncluttered hierarchy, no visual noise |
| **Professional** | Business- or trust-focused sections |
| **Luxury** | Premium, high-end positioning |
| **Sharp** | Crisp edges, defined structure |
| **Sleek** | Polished, streamlined surfaces |
| **Sophisticated** | Refined, upscale tone |
| **Aspirational** | Elevated lifestyle or outcomes |
| **Trustworthy** | Credibility, proof, reassurance |
| **Editorial** | Magazine-like balance of text and imagery |

### Layout and mood modifiers

Combine with primary styles to narrow the description.

| Style | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| **Bold** | Strong headlines, high visual weight |
| **Text-focused** | Copy-heavy, limited imagery |
| **Image-forward** | Photography or visuals dominate |
| **High-contrast** | Strong light/dark, especially over imagery |
| **Subtle** | Understated details, soft presence |
| **Elegant** | Refined typography and spacing |
| **Corporate** | Formal B2B tone |
| **Warm** | Approachable, inviting feel |
| **Dark** | Dark backgrounds or overlays |
| **Light** | Bright, airy backgrounds |

### Motion and interaction (optional in VISUAL STYLE)

Prefer **NOTES / MODIFIERS** for implementation details. Include here only when motion defines the look.

| Style | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| **Animated** | Entrance or scroll-driven motion |
| **Parallax** | Depth and layered scroll effect |
| **Interactive** | Hover states, filters, tabs, carousels |
| **Static** | No motion; calm presentation |

### Proven combinations (used in this codebase)

| VISUAL STYLE |
|--------------|
| Modern, minimal, luxury, and clean |
| Modern, minimal, and clean |
| Modern, minimal, professional, and clean |
| Modern, minimal, professional, and editorial |
