### Styles to avoid (off-brand for this template)

Use only when deliberately diverging from the site system:

- Colorful, playful, funky, retro, grungy, maximalist, cartoonish, busy, cluttered

### CURSOR INFO field reference

When documenting a section component, use all fields consistently:

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **SECTION TYPE** | Short phrase: what the section is |
| **BEST FOR** | Page or use case fit |
| **VISUAL STYLE** | Design adjectives from this guide |
| **LAYOUT** | Structure: split, centered, grid, full-width, etc. |
| **CONTENT ELEMENTS** | Concrete items inside the section |
| **CONVERSION ROLE** | Goal: leads, trust, navigation, sign-up, etc. |
| **IDEAL POSITION** | Placement on the page |
| **NOTES / MODIFIERS** | Responsive behavior, parallax, animations, optional props |

### Rules

1. **Match the real component** — do not label a section "luxury" if the markup and styles are utilitarian.
2. **Stay consistent** — similar sections should share similar VISUAL STYLE values so page-building can match them reliably.
3. **Keep it scannable** — phrases and comma-separated lists only; no sentences in VISUAL STYLE.
4. **Styling must represent the component, not site-contetn.md** 
